    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Steps</p>
      <h2>What happens next</h2>
      <p class="lede">The hardest part is that the weak link is rarely obvious. It fails quietly, in meetings you are not in, and shows up later as stalled pipeline, lost deals, weak renewals or missed expansion.</p>

      {/* Four steps, each with an objective and something the reader
          actually gets. The book is specific that a next step needs a
          defined objective and a stated deliverable, and that a page which
          stops at "get in touch" fumbles at the goal line. */}
      <ol class="steps">
        <li>
          <b>Find your weak link.</b>
          <span>Nine questions, about three minutes. You get a shape across nine dimensions, the one costing you most, and the edge to start with. <a href="/assessment/">Start it here</a>.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <b>Check the dates.</b>
          <span>Five cities, first-class rooms, three hours plus the meal. <a href="#dates">See where and when</a>.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <b>Register.</b>
          <span>{HAS_REGISTRATION
            ? 'Each city is its own event. Limited to twenty-five participants, approved in advance, to keep the conversation relevant and at the right level.'
            : 'Each city is its own event. Limited to twenty-five participants, approved in advance, to keep the conversation relevant and at the right level. Registration opens city by city, so check the dates for the one nearest you.'}</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <b>Ask us anything.</b>
          <span>{FACULTY.map((f, i) => (
            <>{i > 0 ? (i === FACULTY.length - 1 ? ' or ' : ', ') : ''}<a href={`/faculty/#${f.name.split(' ')[0].toLowerCase()}`}>{f.name.split(' ')[0]}</a></>
          ))} will answer directly. No form, no queue.</span>
        </li>
      </ol>

      <div class="cta-pair">
        <a class="btn" href="/assessment/">Find your weak link</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/work-with-us/">Bring The Enterprise Edge in-house</a>
      </div>
